  "title": "Number of Visible People in a Queue",
  "category": "Stack",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "problemStatement": "There are n people standing in a queue, each having a distinct height. For every person, determine how many people to their right are visible. A person j is visible to person i if: j > i Every person between i and j has a height smaller than both person i and person j. Return an array where the i-th element is the number of people visible to the right of person i.",
  "input": "Integer n Array heights",
  "output": "An array of n integers.",
  "constraints": "1 <= n <= 10^5 1 <= heights[i] <= 10^5 All heights are distinct."
